---
description: Label definitions
alwaysApply: true
---

INVOICE
A bill requesting payment for goods or services.
Typical signals (any strong subset is enough):
- Title or heading: Invoice, INV, Tax Invoice, Freight Invoice, Carrier Invoice, Billing Invoice
- Invoice / INV / PRO / billing number
- Bill To / Invoice To / Customer
- Line items with amounts
- Subtotal, tax, freight, total due, amount due, balance due
- Payment terms, due date
A PRO number plus billed amounts is still an invoice, even if a BOL is attached.

CREDIT_NOTE
Credit memo / credit invoice / credit note reducing what is owed.
Look for: Credit Note, Credit Memo, Credit Invoice, CM number, amount credited.
If it is clearly issuing a credit, use CREDIT_NOTE even if "invoice" also appears.

STATEMENT
Account statement, aging, open-invoices listing, balance listing, or monthly statement.
It lists several invoices or a running balance. It is NOT a single invoice requesting payment for one job/shipment.
Do NOT call a single freight invoice a STATEMENT just because it shows previous balance or aging lines, if the main page is still one invoice.

BOL
Bill of Lading / BOL / B/L / Waybill used as the MAIN document.
Shipping contract: shipper, consignee, carrier, commodity, pieces/weight, no request for payment as the primary purpose.
Use BOL ONLY if there is no invoice and no credit note in the file.
A BOL attached behind an invoice does NOT make the file a BOL.

PACKING_LIST
Packing slip / packing list / pick list / contents list as the MAIN document.
Item list for shipping/receiving, usually without amount due / total due as the purpose of the page.
Use PACKING_LIST ONLY if there is no invoice and no credit note.
A packing list behind an invoice does NOT make the file a PACKING_LIST.

TERMS
Terms and conditions, legal, warranty, or rate-tariff legal text as the MAIN document.
Use TERMS ONLY if there is no invoice and no credit note.

BLANK
Empty, unreadable, or no meaningful commercial content (logos/headers only, garbage OCR, whitespace).

OTHER
Anything else: correspondence, quote, PO only, check stub, screenshot, unrelated form.
Use OTHER when it is clearly not one of the labels above.
